 "details": {
  "title": "Misty",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Bing Crosby’s record in his key, B (C♯ for the trumpet), concert E3 to C5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 68. It keeps Crosby’s ways with the tune: “Look at me” a little late each time, “hand” held on F♯ instead of the printed D♯, rests where he rests and the guitar answers, and the last word a bar late. The low D♯ of the rising triplets in each A is below the trumpet and is left out; the triplets start on the E. A short line leads in over the intro, and the ending comes down A, G, F♯, E, D♯, C♯ to A♯, the note the tune starts on.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Erroll Garner, words by Johnny Burke (1954)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, as Bing Crosby phrases it on his record and on the Fret Finder page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "B major concert (C♯ for the trumpet), Crosby’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Four-bar intro, A A B A, the last word a bar late, four-bar ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (misty-guitar.mp3), 2:29"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The four intro bars come first, so bar 1 of the Fret Finder page is bar 5 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
